WEBVTT

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:00.476
LF: I think I've become a lot more ...

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:06.146
some might call it "mature"
in how I talk to people.

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:09.246
You know, because there are consequences.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.524
Like, if you're just focused
on being yourself,

00:12:11.548 --> 00:12:13.317
you're not focused on anyone else.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:17.866
AG: It's common to think of authenticity
as something that's all about me --

00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:20.128
"How do I express myself in the world?"

00:12:20.605 --> 00:12:23.345
But other people have to be
part of that equation.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:26.119
Authenticity can't exist in a vacuum.

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:30.405
I found in my research that concern
for others is a critical ingredient